@startuml
title UML sequence behaviour — A new filter reaches the database without changing an existing Action
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #344054
  FontColor #101828
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #667085
  FontColor #101828
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}
box "Frontend — Angular SPA (state and API client)" #E0F2FE
  participant "HttpTodoApi" as client
end box
box "Backend — Laravel API (HTTP layer)" #D1FADF
  participant "routes/api.php" as routes
  participant "ListTodosRequest" as req
  participant "TodoController" as ctrl
end box
box "Backend — Laravel Application and Domain" #ECFDF3
  participant "ListTodos" as action
  participant "Todo" as model
end box
box "Backend — Laravel Infrastructure" #FFF4E5
  participant "EloquentTodoRepository" as repo
  database "MySQL database" as db
end box
note over client, db : Illustrative new filter "overdue". Added in this change: TodoStatus case, Todo scope, one repository mapping, one test. Unchanged: every Action (L2-044 criterion 6).
client -> routes : GET /api/v1/todos?status=overdue
routes -> req : Resolve the Form Request for the route
req -> req : Validate status against all TodoStatus cases, including the new case
req -> ctrl : Call the controller method with the TodoStatus value
ctrl -> action : Call ListTodos, unchanged
action -> repo : list(TodoStatus) through the TodoRepository interface
repo -> model : Apply the scope that the repository maps to the new case
model -> db : SELECT with the new scope's conditions
db --> model : Rows
model --> repo : Todos
repo --> action : Todos
action --> ctrl : Todos
ctrl --> client : 200 JSON response
@enduml
